==English==

===Etymology===
From the past participle stem of {{der|en|la|nictitō}}, frequentative form of {{m|la|nictō|t=I wink}} (see {{cog|en|nictate}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈnɪktɪteɪtɪŋ/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[winking]], [[blinking]]
#*'''1975''', {{w|Saul Bellow}}, ''Humboldt's Gift'' [Avon ed., 1976, p. 406]:
#*: But she gave me only a dry look. A blink crossed the table. It even seemed to come from the bottom of her eye upward, like a '''nictitating''' membrane.

